  "## A gospel book of Teilo’s church",
  "This great Latin book of the gospels is one of the treasures of the age of the saints. Its painted pages, with their portraits of the evangelists and their carpet of knotwork, belong to the same world as the Book of Kells and the Lindisfarne Gospels. Some scholars believe it was written in Wales itself, perhaps at Llandeilo Fawr, the church of Saint Teilo in the valley of the Tywi.[[cite:wiki-chad]]",
  "We know that it was at Llandeilo in the ninth century, because of what was written in its margins. One note tells how it was bought by a man called Gelhi, who paid for it with his best horse, and gave it ‘to God and to the altar of Saint Teilo’. Other notes record grants of land within fifteen miles of Llandeilo, and the names of the clergy of Teilo who witnessed them.",
  "## The oldest written Welsh",
